target: mf log
summary: Revision/operation history (default: list)

!! Reference

```
Revision/operation history (default: list)

Usage: mf log [COMMAND]

Commands:
  list      Display the revision/operation history
  head      Print the id of the operation the history is on (what --id targets)
  show      Show full details of one revision (a revision id, or HEAD)
  rollback  Navigate the history with coordinated filesystem moves
  undo      Undo the newest change you made, whichever mechanism that takes
  redo      Take the newest undo back, whichever mechanism that takes
  revert    Undo a revision (or an operation) by writing its inverse at HEAD
  prune     Permanently remove operations from the history (irreversible)
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help
```
